{
  "dom_id": "step-q84830",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=4(y-2)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=0$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(0,2).$",
